    description: "Oscar Wilde's The Picture of Dorian Gray (1891) is the great novel of the Aesthetic movement — Dorian's bargain, Lord Henry's epigrams, and the portrait that carries what Dorian refuses to. Still the most widely read expression of Wilde's philosophy that beauty is the supreme value, and still disturbing in its portrait of what a life devoted entirely to that philosophy looks like. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
    keywords: ['books like The Picture of Dorian Gray Oscar Wilde', 'books like The Picture of Dorian Gray', 'oscar wilde similar books', 'gothic fiction similar books', 'what to read after The Picture of Dorian Gray', 'oscar wilde recommendations'],
