    description: "Evelyn Waugh's Brideshead Revisited (1945) is the great English novel of Catholic aristocracy and lost worlds — Charles Ryder's love for Sebastian Flyte, for Julia Flyte, and for the house Brideshead itself, and the slow working of divine grace through lives that resist it. If you were drawn to its elegiac prose and its portrait of a world in the process of being lost, these novels will find you in the same territory.",
    keywords: ['books like Brideshead Revisited Evelyn Waugh', 'books like Brideshead Revisited', 'evelyn waugh similar books', 'british literary fiction similar books', 'what to read after Brideshead Revisited', 'evelyn waugh recommendations'],
