    description: "The Sound and the Fury tells the same story four times in four different voices — including a non-linear narrator who can't experience time — and produces one of the most devastating portraits of a family's collapse in all of fiction. If Faulkner's formal difficulty and emotional intensity stayed with you, these books share his engagement with Southern history, fragmented consciousness, and grief.",
