    description: "The Iliad is the original war poem — not a celebration of glory but a meditation on its cost, on grief, on the impossibility of understanding why we fight. If Homer's epic moved you, these books share its landscape of war, its portrait of heroism's contradictions, and its conviction that even enemies deserve to be mourned.",
