    description: "Strangers in Their Own Land asks how people come to support politics that seem to work against their interests, and answers with careful ethnography rather than condescension. These 8 books share its effort to understand the American right from the inside, its structural thinking about how politics and economics interact, and its belief that empathy is necessary for political analysis.",
